# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. After editing, restart with `npm start -- --clear`:
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined at BUILD time, so a plain reload keeps stale ones.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Agent ids — one per language. The UI asks which language to talk in and dials the
# match. These are resource identifiers, not credentials; they are safe in a build.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VERBEX_AGENT_ID_EN=your_english_agent_id_here
EXPO_PUBLIC_VERBEX_AGENT_ID_BN=your_bangla_agent_id_here

# Verbex API base. Staging: https://api-stage.verbex.ai
EXPO_PUBLIC_VERBEX_API_BASE=https://api.verbex.ai


# ── Distributing an APK/IPA? This is REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────
# Your own HTTPS endpoint that holds the API key and mints tokens. The app POSTs
# { language } and expects { sessionToken } back — the same contract as the web
# app's /api/verbex-session route, so a deployed web-call-demo-ui works as-is.
#
# Release builds REFUSE to start a call without this (see src/lib/session.ts).
# Must be a public HTTPS URL — a LAN IP only works for a device on your network.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://your-app.vercel.app/api/verbex-session


# ── Local development only ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With no endpoint set, a DEV build mints tokens straight from the device using this
# key. Convenient for `npm start` against a dev client.
#
# This is safe to keep here because src/config.ts reads it behind `__DEV__`, so the
# minifier strips it from release bundles — verified by grepping the compiled
# bytecode. Do not remove that guard, and note .env itself is gitignored.
#
# Current keys start with "API…"; older docs show an "ek_…" prefix. Either is fine.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VERBEX_API_KEY=your_api_key_here

# The LiveKit deployment every Verbex web call connects to. This is a hardcoded
# constant inside @verbex-ai/verbex-js-sdk@1.0.0 — the session token does not carry
# it. Only change it for a different Verbex environment.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_LIVEKIT_URL=
